          %p
            %em> Toby
            \: Don't you have to talk about a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+bicategory"} double bicategory
            to get something nontrivial to fill the squares? I may have this wrong, but that's how I remember it.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
            \: No, a double bicategory is just a double category in which both composition operations are only associative and unital up to isomorphism. Sometimes I feel like “double categories” should really have been called “double 2-categories,” since they have nontrivial 2-cells. So it is true that what Eric is interested in are just the 2-cells in the double category
